WEBVTT

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:04.110
Shugo, shugo!

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:04.780
Shugo, shugo!

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:05.820
Shugo, shugo!

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:08.600
Start it off with a Doki! It's Shugo Chara time!

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:11.650
Oh, no! We've got trouble! 
Look at all those X Eggs!

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:13.940
Ah, who could that shadow be?

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:17.360
You know, Tadase-kun seems 
tense for some reason.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:19.230
What could it all mean?

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:21.190
A big storm's a brewin', I tell ya!

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:22.310
Doki!

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:27.180
Yes! Yes!

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:30.100
Let's go!

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:33.110
Yeah! Yeah!

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.900
Shugo, shugo! Yes!

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:44.600
Swing your arms! Hop, step, jump!

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:49.140
Now start marching straight ahead!

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:52.750
Way too awesome! Yes!

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:56.270
Every dream I've ever had!

00:00:56.620 --> 00:01:01.980
Since they're all actually coming true.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:08.100
What kind of person will I be today?

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:13.390
What counts is being true to yourself!

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:17.540
Going somewhere?

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:19.960
Take it to the finish!

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:23.450
You'll always be able to

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:26.390
unlock your heart.

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:29.350
So keep on changing!

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:31.760
It's so exciting!

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:39.890
Let's go forward, believing in our hearts!

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.620
Straight ahead!

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:44.280
Yeah! Yeah!

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:57.310
I love you, Amu-chan.

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:00.540
I'm going to repeat it every day.

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:02.290
As often as I can.

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:04.990
Enough to make up for the 
days before I even met you.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:08.200
Tadase-kun...

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:10.300
I love you, Amu-chan.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:11.680
I love <i>you</i>.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.720
I was dreaming...

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:23.230
Tadase-kun's even aggressive in my dreams!

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:25.720
It's nice that you're ecstatic 
so early in the morning, but...

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:27.040
Amu-chan...

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:30.220
He's in my bed <i>again</i>?!

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:31.670
Why you little...

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:33.760
He must have been cold.

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:36.100
I am <i>not</i> your 
hot-water bottle, darn it!

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:38.190
Wake up, you stupid cat!

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:50.020
Episode 76
A New Enemy!? Battle on a Moonlit Night!

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:55.730
What am I going to do with him?

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:58.320
How long do you think Ikuto will be with us?

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.490
Well, he doesn't seem to 
be feeling better yet...

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:04.700
And even when he is, 
he's got no place to go.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:06.720
But he can't just...

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:08.310
Can I help you with that?

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:09.410
Ouch!

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:12.890
Amu, are you okay?

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:16.040
I'm fine, honest. I was just 
surprised, is all.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:18.800
I'm sorry. It's my fault for 
speaking to you so suddenly.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:24.080
Were you burned, Amu-chan?

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:30.390
My word, Mrs. Mashiro, don't those two 
youngins make a fine couple?

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:31.700
Yeah...

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:36.840
So, when did you switch 
to calling her Amu-chan, huh?

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:38.380
T-That's...

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:40.130
Something happened, didn't it?

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:41.610
N-No, um...

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:43.520
That flustered reaction is fishy...

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:45.890
Spit it out, ya got me?

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:47.140
What's going on here?

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:49.360
What happened between you two?

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:51.420
Come on, Rima, help me out here!

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:52.370
Talk!

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.330
If you wanna eat katsudon, spit it out!

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:57.730
There's nothing to tell, honest!

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:01.690
Now then, let's begin our meeting.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:04.880
Fujisaki-kun has something to discuss today.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:09.080
You see, last night I heard a strange sound.

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:39.140
I don't know whether it's connected to what I saw...

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:44.440
But for there to be so many people with empty hearts out there...

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:45.930
It's suspicious, no matter how you look at it.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:47.910
It would have to be...

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:49.720
The work of Easter.

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:52.330
I think that's a good possibility.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:56.750
Perhaps they've initiated another 
plan in addition to the ? Eggs.

00:04:56.750 --> 00:05:00.000
? Eggs are confusing enough as it is!

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.930
Regardless, we must all be on guard!

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:06.590
If you sense something strange, 
contact the others immediately.

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:15.780
I wonder if Easter is collecting X Eggs 
again like they did with Black Diamond.

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:20.470
Maybe... Although we don't have much 
to go on this time, so it's hard to be sure.

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:23.340
I'll stop them no matter what!

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:27.260
I'm determined to become stronger,

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:30.520
so that I can protect you and everyone else.

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:35.780
I love you, Amu-chan.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:38.370
I-Is that for today?

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:39.220
Yup!

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:41.440
It's embarrassing but...

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:43.470
I'm so happy!

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:47.970
Those two are off in their 
own little world, aren't they?

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:49.740
It's embarrassing just to watch them.

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:50.640
How undignified...

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:53.390
This feeling...

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:55.480
Amu-chan.

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:00.560
This is...

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:04.480
Look at all of the people with empty hearts!

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:10.770
Did you hear that?

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:12.630
It sounded like a guitar.

00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:13.440
No.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:15.870
It's the A string of a violin.

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:17.380
A violin?

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:18.740
Could it be Ikuto?

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:23.630
No way... He's sleeping in my room 
because he isn't feeling well.

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:26.620
The sound came from 
over there, didn't it?

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:27.760
Amu-chan!

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:36.560
No one's here.

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:40.090
It's starting to get dark, too. 
I think we should go home for today.

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:40.750
But...

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:44.120
We can't feel the presence 
of the X Eggs anymore, either.

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:46.820
Who on Earth would be 
collecting so many eggs?

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:52.550
There is a method of plucking a 
violin's string called "pizzicato."

00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:56.060
I've known that sound since I was a boy.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:59.600
If he's actually behind this...

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:01.140
I won't forgive him.

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:03.970
Tadase-kun...

00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:06.910
Shall we head home?

00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:08.450
S-Sure.

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:12.590
Tadase-kun is always so gentle and kind.

00:07:12.590 --> 00:07:15.480
So why does he get that look 
in his eyes when he talks about Ikuto?

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:20.750
What could have happened between those two?

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:28.680
Ikuto...

00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:35.360
Hey, Ikuto... Did you go out 
at all while I was gone?

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:37.240
Huh? Where would I go?

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:39.180
Oh, um, never mind.

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:48.610
You must be hungry. How about I go buy 
some onigiri at the convenience store?

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:51.060
Don't want any. I'm going to sleep.

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:52.680
Hey!

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:54.980
W-What's with that attitude?

00:07:54.980 --> 00:07:56.450
Now, now...

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:58.180
He plays by his own tune.

00:07:58.180 --> 00:07:59.940
He's a cat after all.

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:01.460
Ikuto...

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:09.350
The fine-tuning of the equipment 
has been proceeding well.

00:08:09.350 --> 00:08:14.310
There were responses from last night's 
and this afternoon's activation tests.

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:18.420
Tonight, we will commence the Death Rebel plan.

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:20.560
I have high expectations of you.

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:22.100
Leave everything to me.

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:29.860
Preparations are complete.

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:31.260
All right, let's get started!

00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:31.980
Okay!

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:45.060
That tuning fork contains a special waveform.

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:51.720
When struck, the waves travel to the violin we 
infused with X Egg energy and resonate.

00:08:57.450 --> 00:08:59.950
And Ikuto becomes my puppet.

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:05.890
Hey, Ikuto!

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:12.090
Tadase.

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:16.730
I had my suspicions after what happened 
this afternoon, and I was right!

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:26.890
It was you after all, wasn't it?

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:29.060
Tsukiyomi Ikuto!

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:41.140
If Ikuto plays the violin, the energy becomes 
amplified and collects a great number of X Eggs.

00:09:42.210 --> 00:09:46.640
In this way, we will lure out the Embryo.

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:48.560
Ikuto!

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:51.310
That's enough, Tsukiyomi Ikuto!

00:09:55.270 --> 00:09:57.290
Be careful, Tadase!

00:09:57.290 --> 00:09:59.820
He's Character Transformed into 
something I've never seen before!

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:12.880
The violin transformed?

00:10:28.950 --> 00:10:33.100
Tsukiyomi Ikuto, I won't let you 
do as you please any longer!

00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:39.360
Say something, Tsukiyomi Ikuto!

00:10:48.610 --> 00:10:53.080
Good grief, how many times 
will I have to tell him?

00:10:54.390 --> 00:10:55.830
Hey!

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:03.420
Blood? He's hurt?

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:06.260
How?

00:11:21.050 --> 00:11:23.040
What's the matter, Amu-chan?

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:25.060
Thinking hard about something for a change?

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:30.140
When did Ikuto get hurt like that?

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:33.460
Was it there before he went to sleep?

00:11:34.350 --> 00:11:35.930
Here comes Tadase-kun!

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:38.510
Tadase-k-

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:45.430
He looks kind of scary right now.

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:48.770
Good morning, Amu-chan.

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:50.960
Good morning.

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:54.860
Tadase-kun's hurt, too?

00:11:57.340 --> 00:11:58.920
Is something wrong?

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:00.040
No...

00:12:00.520 --> 00:12:01.810
Shall we go?

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:12.600
There's <i>definitely</i> something 
weird about that violin-nya.

00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:19.070
What should I do-nya?!

00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:22.720
Do I seriously have no choice 
but to talk to those guys-nya?

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:33.990
About the increase in hearts' eggs 
being stolen, which we discussed yesterday...

00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:36.900
I know who's behind drawing them out.

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:37.970
Really?

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:40.680
It's Tsukiyomi Ikuto.

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:45.270
I saw him last night.

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:51.640
He was surrounded by many X Eggs and had Character 
Transformed into something I'd never seen before.

00:13:06.710 --> 00:13:10.800
Tsukiyomi Ikuto, I won't let you 
do as you please any longer!

00:13:14.070 --> 00:13:16.770
Say something, Tsukiyomi Ikuto!

00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:44.850
Wait!

00:14:02.430 --> 00:14:07.370
So Easter is making him 
collect X Eggs, then?

00:14:07.370 --> 00:14:08.340
But...

00:14:09.230 --> 00:14:11.010
What is it, Amu-chan?

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:17.840
That's right... If I say that Ikuto's staying 
at my house, then he'll find out that he...

00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:21.970
Do you know something about him?

00:14:21.970 --> 00:14:23.770
No, um...

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:25.390
Amu-chan?

00:14:29.110 --> 00:14:33.510
Did something happen between you 
and Ikuto in the past, Tadase-kun?

00:14:34.690 --> 00:14:38.410
Whenever someone mentions him, you get so...

00:14:54.520 --> 00:14:56.390
Okay!

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:58.550
That's enough about that!

00:14:58.550 --> 00:15:00.320
Time to get to work!

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:03.600
Yaya-tan can't handle tense 
situations like this-dechu.

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:07.430
Our mission today is to sow the flower garden!

00:15:07.430 --> 00:15:10.940
Once we're finished, everyone's 
dismissed, so let's get cracking!

00:15:10.940 --> 00:15:12.620
Yeah!

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:14.470
Y-Yeah...

00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:17.550
Amu-chan.

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:20.700
Shall we walk home together 
once we're done?

00:15:22.950 --> 00:15:23.980
Sure.

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:29.770
What's with you-dechu?

00:15:29.770 --> 00:15:31.630
All hands, assemble!

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:36.280
We finally know who the culprit is and they're planting seeds!

00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:37.650
It's shameful!

00:15:37.650 --> 00:15:42.020
So, instead of those losers, we'll have to search 
for that vagabond Tsukiyomi Ikuto ourselves!

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:44.730
Hey! What's with this lackadaisical attitude?!

00:15:44.730 --> 00:15:47.290
You're the only one who wants to, Kiseki-tan-dechu.

00:15:47.290 --> 00:15:49.670
Ran, Miki, and Su took off!

00:15:49.670 --> 00:15:51.970
Those disobedient...

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:56.520
It would have been better to tell everyone 
about Ikuto at the meeting, I think.

00:15:56.520 --> 00:15:57.680
But...

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:01.220
Since Tadase-kun hates Ikuto so much...

00:16:01.220 --> 00:16:04.640
If he finds out that Ikuto-san 
is staying in Amu-chan's room...

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:07.980
I hate you, Amu-chan!

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:10.540
And I'm going to tell you that every day.

00:16:10.540 --> 00:16:13.470
Enough to make up for the days 
before I even met you!

00:16:14.960 --> 00:16:17.430
He'd clearly hate her for it.

00:16:17.430 --> 00:16:19.470
I'll never tell!

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:21.510
What can't you tell?

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:25.300
Oh, it's you, Nagihiko.

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:27.730
Worried about something?

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:30.050
It's not so much worry as...

00:16:30.050 --> 00:16:31.900
If you need to talk, 
I'd be happy to listen.

00:16:34.030 --> 00:16:37.020
Hey, Nagihiko, could you do me a favor?

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:41.680
Amu-chan, isn't this...

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:44.060
Nadeshiko!

00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:45.530
You like this?

00:16:45.530 --> 00:16:47.130
Yes, yes, yes!

00:16:47.130 --> 00:16:49.560
Can you talk like a girl for me?

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:51.580
Um...

00:16:51.580 --> 00:16:54.100
What might be troubling you, Amu-chan?

00:16:55.450 --> 00:16:58.810
Nadeshiko!

00:16:57.090 --> 00:16:58.810
Amu-chan, calm down!

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:04.060
Hey, look at that.

00:17:05.110 --> 00:17:06.380
It's Yoru!

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:10.060
You can't just go wandering around!

00:17:10.060 --> 00:17:12.020
What's the matter?

00:17:12.020 --> 00:17:15.060
I have something I need to 
talk to you guys about-nya.

00:17:15.060 --> 00:17:16.130
With us?

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:18.960
You see... Um...

00:17:18.960 --> 00:17:19.520
Ikuto is-

00:17:19.740 --> 00:17:21.720
Good work, commoners!

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:27.640
You anticipated your King's orders and 
captured Tsukiyomi Ikuto's accomplice!

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:29.390
Anticipated?

00:17:29.390 --> 00:17:30.600
Accomplice?

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:32.060
Captured?

00:17:33.810 --> 00:17:35.180
You mean me?!

00:17:35.180 --> 00:17:38.900
Now, tell us where Tsukiyomi 
Ikuto is! Out with it!

00:17:38.900 --> 00:17:40.500
Time to play interrogation-dechu!

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:42.180
Sounds super fun!

00:17:42.430 --> 00:17:45.930
This is bad. If everyone finds 
out where Ikuto is...

00:17:45.930 --> 00:17:48.280
Tadase-kun will definitely...

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:51.890
I have a bad feeling about this-nya.

00:17:52.600 --> 00:17:54.930
Yoru, how could you?!

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:55.800
Hey, stop struggling!

00:17:54.930 --> 00:17:56.100
Desu!

00:17:58.770 --> 00:18:00.640
Darn, he got away!

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:01.870
Damn him!

00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:03.180
In pursuit-dechu.

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:10.060
Hopefully that lets 
Yoru get away for now...

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:12.650
But where will he escape to?

00:18:13.140 --> 00:18:15.180
Amu-chan's house!

00:18:17.680 --> 00:18:19.750
I hope I never have to 
go through that again-nya.

00:18:19.750 --> 00:18:22.060
I didn't even get a chance 
to talk to them-nya.

00:18:26.860 --> 00:18:27.680
Pass!

00:18:27.930 --> 00:18:30.340
All right, all right!

00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:33.810
Hm? {No way. It's not a word used by English-speakers, and we've been working hard to make it sound natural. I suggest either "hm" or just leave it unsubbed completely since it's not even a word but a sound.}

00:18:34.560 --> 00:18:36.860
What the heck's wrong with you-nya?!

00:18:36.860 --> 00:18:39.750
You can't go back to Amu-chan's house!

00:18:39.750 --> 00:18:42.540
You've gotta stay on the run 
until they give up the chase!

00:18:42.540 --> 00:18:45.100
But I need to talk to 
you guys, remember-nya?!

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:46.640
What does that matter?

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:48.340
But it's...

00:18:48.340 --> 00:18:51.760
If people realize that Ikuto-san 
is here we'll all be in trouble!

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:54.820
Don't cause Amu-chan any more grief!

00:18:56.760 --> 00:19:00.750
Fine, I got it-nya! I won't rely 
on you guys anymore-nya!

00:19:00.750 --> 00:19:03.050
Where did that rapscallion go?

00:19:03.050 --> 00:19:06.110
I thought I felt his presence 
around here, but...

00:19:06.890 --> 00:19:08.360
There he is-dechu!

00:19:09.390 --> 00:19:12.250
Looks like it's time for 
desperate measures-nya.

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:15.220
Run away, run away! 
Run far, far away-nya!

00:19:15.790 --> 00:19:17.100
Wait!

00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:18.930
Wait-dechu!

00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:24.520
Seems we're out of the woods.

00:19:24.520 --> 00:19:26.020
Keeping a secret...

00:19:26.020 --> 00:19:27.920
...sure is tiring.

00:19:28.470 --> 00:19:29.890
Hiding something?

00:19:30.360 --> 00:19:31.700
Yeah.

00:19:31.700 --> 00:19:34.520
Say you're hiding something from 
someone important to you,

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:40.100
but if you told, it would make that 
person angry or even hate you.

00:19:40.100 --> 00:19:42.060
What would you do if it were you, Nagihiko?

00:19:45.900 --> 00:19:48.560
I don't think keeping 
secrets is a good idea.

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:49.660
But...

00:19:50.940 --> 00:19:54.040
There are some things that 
are best kept hidden.

00:19:54.350 --> 00:19:58.030
By doing that, you may be preventing their feelings from being hurt,

00:19:58.030 --> 00:20:02.950
but you have to be willing to face the suffering that comes from living with a lie.

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:08.600
If you're going to lie, you have 
to be prepared for that.

00:20:09.190 --> 00:20:10.610
Prepared?

00:20:12.220 --> 00:20:15.690
What should I do?

00:20:18.290 --> 00:20:19.430
Amu-chan?

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:22.900
What's the matter? You seem distracted.

00:20:22.900 --> 00:20:24.180
Tired?

00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:26.700
No, I'm fine.

00:20:28.920 --> 00:20:31.030
Excuse me. 
Could you wait here?

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:37.440
A present?

00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:38.070
Yeah.

00:20:38.470 --> 00:20:41.010
These are my grandmother's favorite flowers.

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:43.790
I was hoping they'd make 
her feel better, if only a little.

00:20:43.790 --> 00:20:45.720
Is she sick?

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:48.110
She had a fall about two years ago.

00:20:48.110 --> 00:20:49.510
She hasn't been the same since.

00:20:49.970 --> 00:20:51.420
I see.

00:20:51.420 --> 00:20:52.970
That sounds rough.

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:55.940
No, she's quite tenacious.

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:58.520
She gets angry if people 
worry about her too much.

00:20:59.180 --> 00:21:02.120
But because she's like that...

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:06.030
Seeing how frail she's become...

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:08.220
It's a bit hard on me, I guess.

00:21:12.290 --> 00:21:14.030
Flowers are amazing, don't you think?

00:21:14.030 --> 00:21:14.850
Yeah.

00:21:15.530 --> 00:21:19.460
They're so tiny, but they use 
all their strength to bloom.

00:21:20.320 --> 00:21:23.940
And because of their efforts, 
they make people smile.

00:21:23.940 --> 00:21:27.020
I want to be like that.

00:21:28.630 --> 00:21:32.350
Tadase-kun is kind and strong.

00:21:34.590 --> 00:21:38.890
I don't want to keep secrets from him!

00:21:39.910 --> 00:21:41.170
Tadase-kun.

00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:45.470
Um, about Ikuto...

00:21:47.840 --> 00:21:49.060
Um...

00:21:49.460 --> 00:21:53.250
I don't think he's such a bad person.

00:21:53.250 --> 00:21:55.180
What am I saying?

00:21:55.180 --> 00:21:56.210
Amu-chan.

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:00.290
Let me tell you something.

00:22:00.290 --> 00:22:04.480
Tsukiyomi Ikuto is a black cat who brings nothing but misfortune.

00:22:10.170 --> 00:22:12.380
Misfortune?

00:22:12.380 --> 00:22:13.790
Black cat?

00:22:22.300 --> 00:22:26.170
We'll walk this path,

00:22:26.170 --> 00:22:29.960
no matter what may happen.

00:22:30.290 --> 00:22:34.250
Because when we combine our strength,

00:22:34.250 --> 00:22:38.170
something's bound to change!

00:22:46.040 --> 00:22:53.480
You're always so quick to say "absolutely,"

00:22:53.990 --> 00:22:57.850
but shouldn't you think it through a bit first?

00:22:58.220 --> 00:23:01.230
Can't you at least do that???

00:23:02.300 --> 00:23:05.980
You know, I'm starting to understand

00:23:05.980 --> 00:23:09.440
the delicate movements of the heart.

00:23:09.880 --> 00:23:16.900
My own abilities aren't really all that special...

00:23:18.210 --> 00:23:22.200
But even if the first shot's off the mark

00:23:22.200 --> 00:23:26.070
the third'll bravely hit the bull's-eye!

00:23:28.180 --> 00:23:32.160
We'll walk this path,

00:23:32.160 --> 00:23:35.780
even if it's a steep climb.

00:23:36.240 --> 00:23:40.250
Because when we put our hearts together

00:23:40.250 --> 00:23:44.200
something definitely changes!

00:23:50.590 --> 00:23:51.970
This is bad!

00:23:51.970 --> 00:23:53.230
What is it, Amu-chan?

00:23:53.230 --> 00:23:57.980
A date with Tadase-kun! A date with Tadase-kun! A date with Tadase-kun!

00:23:56.900 --> 00:23:58.970
Amu-chan, calm down!

00:23:57.980 --> 00:23:59.590
Oh man, what should I wear?

00:23:59.590 --> 00:24:01.210
How should I do my hair?

00:24:00.520 --> 00:24:03.000
Amu-chan, it's time to go.

00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:05.610
Where should we go? 
What should we talk about?

00:24:05.610 --> 00:24:08.870
Date! Date! Date!

00:24:10.060 --> 00:24:12.600
Next time on Shugo Chara!! Doki:

00:24:12.600 --> 00:24:15.120
Shocking! First Date, Busted!?

00:24:15.120 --> 00:24:16.750
Wait, what's "busted" supposed to mean?!

00:24:16.750 --> 00:24:18.560
Would you please calm down?
